; QRX 22.5.12 live scenario: ReactOS Solitaire and the DirectDraw test program in
; their own Intuition window / screen, operated with real input events
; (QRXInput -> input.device).
; No Wanderer: starting it sporadically hung AROS m68k in FS-UAE (grey display,
; seen before any QRX program ran).  qrx-win32 opens the Workbench screen itself.
FailAt 1000
Assign QRX: SYS:QRX >NIL:
CD SYS:X86
Run >QRXOUT:live-sol.out QRX:C/qrx-win32 -v -L QRXOUT:live-sol.log sol.exe
Wait 900
QRX:C/QRXScreenGrab QRXOUT:sol-1-start.ppm >QRXOUT:grab1.txt
; deal from the deck (top left of the card table)
QRX:C/QRXInput click 80 135
Wait 300
QRX:C/QRXScreenGrab QRXOUT:sol-2-dealt.ppm >QRXOUT:grab2.txt
QRX:C/QRXInput click 80 135
Wait 60
QRX:C/QRXScreenGrab QRXOUT:sol-3-dealt2.ppm >QRXOUT:grab3.txt
; DirectDraw test program: 640x480x8 exclusive mode -> its own 8-bit screen.
; Started synchronously: a Run-started process hangs in OpenScreen on this AROS
; build (OpenScreen itself works, see TESTREPORT); -G captures the display.
QRX:C/qrx-win32 -v -L QRXOUT:live-dx.log -G QRXOUT:dx-screen.ppm 10 dxtest.exe 12 >QRXOUT:live-dx.out
QRX:C/QRXScreenGrab QRXOUT:after-dx.ppm >QRXOUT:grab4.txt
Copy SYS:X86/dxtest.log QRXOUT:dxtest-live.log
Echo "done" >QRXOUT:DONE
